\begin_layout Standard
This thesis started from a personal question:
 
\emph on
can a person with no background in quantum computing learn its basic ideas by building and studying a small interactive game?

\emph default
 I came from the world GNU Linux system administration,
 and quantum computing was a subject that I did not know at all.
 To answer the question I created a memory game in which every card is produced by quantum measurements,
 and I added five experiments,
 each showing a different kind of entanglement between two qubits.
 The same code was run on a simulator and on a real IBM quantum processor.
 This chapter summarizes what the experiments showed,
 the practical limits met when working with real hardware,
 the role of artificial intelligence in the project,
 and what the work has meant for my learning.
\end_layout

